rf_writer+0x3cd/0x418()

These warnings are due to conflicting kernel boot variables, and is
expected behavior if you have both rcupdate.rcu_normal (which tells RCU
to never do expedited grace periods) and rcuperf.gp_exp (which tells
rcuperf to only test expedited grace periods.  The rcuperf kernel module
complains about the conflict.  It will also complain about the opposite
combination of rcupdate.rcu_expedited and !rcuperf.gp_exp.

							Thanx, Paul

